# The sniff tree PAX carries as /bin/sniff (sn04; tools/mksniff builds it).
#
# sniff is the gdb-language debugger in wolf (wolffe-lang/sniff, Track 21). On PAX it
# starts its own child and traces it with PAX's ptrace(2) (px102), the same Linux
# requests, wait statuses and register layout as on Linux; the S2 session typed at
# the console is held to the Linux transcript (sniff notes/sn04-sniff-on-pax.md).
# PAX loads only static ET_EXEC files, so sniff and every program it debugs there are static.
#
# SNIFF_REV is sniff's trunk 6dd382d (2026-11-09: list, help, watchpoints and conditions, threads, signals, attach,
# -p; wolf 0.2.38), set when the SSH stick was cut (px97f).
SNIFF_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/sniff
SNIFF_REV=6dd382d4efc41ce1c75cb977498ddbb62786b546

# Codeload source archive sha256 at SNIFF_REV, read twice when the pin is set.
SNIFF_SOURCE_SHA256=c7f638ad3bb0a2fbd14a92aa04a8b1389d34e2b33c90fb461f0fbe31646d5742
